        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): bound stalled diagnostic response reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Telegram diagnostics and membership audits could keep waiting after the Bot API returned response headers but then stalled or only trickled the response body.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTelegram Bot API diagnostic body reads now use a Telegram-local bounded reader with the existing byte cap, a per-chunk idle timeout, and an overall body deadline. The change covers `getMe`, best-effort `getWebhookInfo`, and membership-audit `getChatMember` reads without changing fetch/header timeout or webhook best-effort semantics.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTelegram setup checks and membership audits now fail or degrade on a bounded deadline instead of appearing to spin forever on a stuck response body.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/response-body-timeout.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/probe.response-body-timeout.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/probe.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/audit.test.ts` (22 tests passed)\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n- Claude autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n",
